You're likely using the old message structure where `message.content` is a string. In v7, messages use a `parts` array to support tool calls, reasoning, and other content types.

Update your UI to iterate over `message.parts` and handle each part type:

```tsx
{messages.map(message => (
  <div key={message.id}>
    {message.parts.map((part, i) => {
      switch (part.type) {
        case 'text':
          return <div key={i}>{part.text}</div>;
        case 'tool-call':
          return <pre key={i}>{JSON.stringify(part, null, 2)}</pre>;
        case 'tool-result':
          return <pre key={i}>{JSON.stringify(part, null, 2)}</pre>;
        case 'reasoning':
          return <div key={i}>{part.text}</div>;
        // Add other part types as needed
      }
    })}
  </div>
))}
```

[7] explains that tool calls and reasoning appear as typed parts in the `parts` array, not as `message.content`.

Use the `throttle` option to reduce the frequency of UI updates during streaming:

