To attach the model ID and token usage to each assistant message, use the `messageMetadata` callback in `toUIMessageStream`. Here's how to do it:

### Server-side (Route Handler)
```ts
import {
  createUIMessageStreamResponse,
  toUIMessageStream,
} from 'ai';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages } = await req.json();

  const result = await agent.stream({
    messages: await convertToModelMessages(messages),
  });

  return createUIMessageStreamResponse({
    stream: toUIMessageStream({
      stream: result.stream,
      messageMetadata: ({ part }) => {
        // Attach model ID when the message starts
        if (part.type === 'start') {
          return { modelId: 'gpt-4' };
        }

        // Attach token usage when the message finishes
        if (part.type === 'finish-step') {
          return { usage: part.usage };
        }
      },
    }),
  });
}
```

### Client-side (UI Component)
```tsx
'use client';

import { useChat } from '@ai-sdk/react';

export default function Chat() {
  const { messages } = useChat();

  return (
    <div>
      {messages.map((m) => (
        <div key={m.id}>
          <strong>{m.role}:</strong>
          {m.parts.map((p, i) => p.type === 'text' && <span key={i}>{p.text}</span>)}

          {/* Display model ID */}
          {m.metadata?.modelId && (
            <div>Model: {m.metadata.modelId}</div>
          )}

          {/* Display token usage */}
          {m.metadata?.usage && (
            <div>
              Tokens: {m.metadata.usage.inputTokens} in,{' '}
              {m.metadata.usage.outputTokens} out,{' '}
              {m.metadata.usage.totalTokens} total
            </div>
          )}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Key points:**
- The `messageMetadata` callback receives each part of the message stream
- Return metadata objects for specific part types ('start', 'finish-step', etc.)
- Token usage is available in the `usage` property of 'finish-step' parts
- Metadata is automatically attached to the message and sent to the client
- Access metadata on the client via `message.metadata`[1][2][3]

Only `image/*` and `text/*` content types are automatically converted into multi-modal content parts when using `sendMessage({ text, files })`. PDFs (`application/pdf`) are not included in this automatic conversion, so the model ignores them [2].

To send PDFs, you need to manually convert them to data URLs and include them in the `parts` array:

```tsx
const fileParts = await Promise.all(
  Array.from(files).map(async file => ({
    type: 'file' as const,
    filename: file.name,
    mediaType: file.type,
    url: await new Promise<string>((resolve, reject) => {
      const reader = new FileReader();
      reader.onload = () => resolve(reader.result as string);
      reader.onerror = reject;
      reader.readAsDataURL(file);
    }),
  }))
);

sendMessage({
  role: 'user',
  parts: [{ type: 'text', text: input }, ...fileParts],
});
```

This approach is shown in the PDF chat cookbook example [6,8].

In the `onFinish` callback of `useChat`, the event object includes three boolean flags that tell you why the response ended:

- `isAbort`: true when the user clicked the stop button
- `isDisconnect`: true when the network dropped or the client disconnected
- `isError`: true when an error occurred

Example:
```tsx
const { messages } = useChat({
  onFinish: ({ isAbort, isDisconnect, isError }) => {
    if (isAbort) console.log('User clicked stop');
    if (isDisconnect) console.log('Network dropped or client disconnected');
    if (isError) console.log('An error occurred');
  },
});
```

