When you enable resumable streams with `resume: true`, the `stop()` function only aborts the current client request (HTTP connection), not the server-side generation. The server keeps the stream running to allow reconnection later, so the model continues using tokens [1][2][3][4].

To stop the model, you need a dedicated server endpoint that:
1. Persists the partial assistant message
2. Cancels the server-side work
3. Clears the active stream reference

Client-side:
```tsx
const chat = useChat({
  id: chatId,
  resume: true,
});

async function stopStream() {
  await fetch(`/api/chat/${chatId}/stop`, { method: 'POST' });
  chat.stop(); // Only stops the local client stream
}
```

Server-side:
```ts
// app/api/chat/[id]/stop/route.ts
export async function POST(req: Request, { params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {
  const { id } = await params;
  const body = await req.json();

  if (body.activeStreamId) {
    await cancelActiveWork(body.activeStreamId); // Your cancellation logic
    await saveChat({ id, activeStreamId: null });
  }

  return Response.json({ success: true });
}
```

See [Stop an Active Resumable Stream](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/chatbot-resume-streams#stop-an-active-resumable-stream) for full implementation details [2][6][7][8].

Use `enum` output mode to force a single classification. On the client, define a schema with a field whose value is an enum of the three categories. On the server, return that single choice with `Output.choice`.

Client (React):
```tsx
'use client';

import { useObject } from '@ai-sdk/react';
import { z } from 'zod';

export default function ClassifyTicket() {
  const { object, submit, isLoading } = useObject({
    api: '/api/classify-ticket',
    schema: z.object({ type: z.enum(['bug', 'feature', 'question']) }),
  });

  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => submit('The login button does nothing')} disabled={isLoading}>
        Classify ticket
      </button>
      {object && <div>Type: {object.type}</div>}
    </>
  );
}
```

Server (Next.js route):
```ts
import { createTextStreamResponse, Output, streamText, toTextStream } from 'ai';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const context = await req.json();

  const result = streamText({
    model: 'anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5',
    output: Output.choice({ options: ['bug', 'feature', 'question'] }),
    prompt: `Classify this support ticket as exactly one of: bug, feature, question.
    Ticket: ${context}`,
  });

  return createTextStreamResponse({
    stream: toTextStream({ stream: result.stream }),
  });
}
```

To enforce exactly 5 items, set both `minItems` and `maxItems` to 5 in `Output.array()`:

